%%entity WashBay help: One physical wash or detailing bay with its own capacity, availability, equipment and operating restrictions.
%%entity WashBay icon: Warehouse
%%field WashBay.site_id help: Operating site that controls the physical wash bay.
%%field WashBay.equipment_id help: Primary machine or conveyor serving this bay, when fitted.
%%field WashBay.bay_code help: Stable printed lane identifier, unique across the business.
%%field WashBay.name help: Name supervisors use to dispatch vehicles to the correct lane.
%%field WashBay.capacity_vehicles help: Maximum vehicles safely handled simultaneously in this bay.
%%field WashBay.status help: Current operating availability; operators must not allocate a closed or maintenance bay.
%%field WashBay.is_active help: Deactivate the bay to block future allocations while preserving its history.
%%field WashBay.access_notes help: Clearance, size, safe-entry and operating limitations staff must follow.
%%field WashBay.status enum: BayStatus
%%section entity: WashBay; name: Bay identification; help: Which site and machine this lane belongs to, and what capacity operators can schedule.; rows: bay_code, name | site_id, equipment_id | capacity_vehicles
%%section entity: WashBay; name: Availability and clearance; help: Whether the bay may be allocated and any restrictions staff must follow.; rows: is_active,access_notes
%%entity BayAllocation help: A reserved interval for one vehicle in one bay, tied to the booking or delivered work order and updated when service begins and ends.
%%entity BayAllocation icon: CalendarClock
%%field BayAllocation.wash_bay_id help: Bay reserved for the vehicle during the stated interval.
%%field BayAllocation.booking_id help: Customer reservation that originated the slot, if any.
%%field BayAllocation.work_order_id help: Service job occupying the bay, if already created.
%%field BayAllocation.vehicle_id help: Actual vehicle scheduled to occupy the bay.
%%field BayAllocation.employee_id help: Worker responsible for dispatch or service at this allocation.
%%field BayAllocation.status help: Reservation, arrival, service and release progress for the slot.
%%field BayAllocation.planned_start help: Scheduled slot start expressed in the site time zone.
%%field BayAllocation.planned_end help: Expected latest release time used for capacity checks.
%%field BayAllocation.actual_start help: Real service-entry time for waiting and throughput metrics.
%%field BayAllocation.actual_end help: Real service-exit time for utilization and delay metrics.
%%field BayAllocation.exception_reason help: Reason for cancellation, late arrival, overrun or no-show.
%%field BayAllocation.status enum: BayAllocationStatus
%%section entity: BayAllocation; name: Reservation; help: The vehicle, bay, assigned worker, and source records for this occupancy.; rows: wash_bay_id, vehicle_id | booking_id, work_order_id | employee_id, planned_start | planned_end
%%section entity: BayAllocation; name: Service evidence; help: Actual occupancy and reasons for a missed or shortened booking.; rows: actual_start,actual_end | exception_reason
%%entity DamageClaim help: A customer claim concerning an incident affecting a vehicle, preserving submitted evidence, adjudication, and final settlement.
%%entity DamageClaim icon: ShieldAlert
%%field DamageClaim.incident_id help: Recorded incident being investigated; claims must retain source evidence.
%%field DamageClaim.customer_id help: Customer making the claim and receiving updates.
%%field DamageClaim.vehicle_id help: Vehicle for which damage is alleged.
%%field DamageClaim.employee_id help: Investigator assigned to gather evidence and document the decision.
%%field DamageClaim.claim_number help: Unique claim reference for insurer and customer correspondence.
%%field DamageClaim.status help: Investigation, decision and settlement state of this claim.
%%field DamageClaim.reported_at help: Time the claim was first received from the customer.
%%field DamageClaim.claimed_amount help: Customer stated amount, not automatically an accepted liability.
%%field DamageClaim.approved_amount help: Amount authorized for settlement after review.
%%field DamageClaim.damage_description help: Specific damage and circumstances reported, preserving the original allegation.
%%field DamageClaim.evidence_reference help: Location or reference of photographs, inspection notes and supporting documents.
%%field DamageClaim.resolution_notes help: Decision reasoning, approvals and customer communication record.
%%field DamageClaim.closed_at help: Time the dispute was finally closed after settlement or rejection.
%%field DamageClaim.status enum: ClaimStatus
%%section entity: DamageClaim; name: Claim intake; help: The incident, claimant, vehicle, investigator, requested amount and observed damage.; rows: claim_number, incident_id | customer_id, vehicle_id | employee_id, reported_at | claimed_amount, damage_description
%%section entity: DamageClaim; name: Decision and settlement; help: Evidence and management decision used to resolve a claim without deleting original facts.; rows: evidence_reference,approved_amount | resolution_notes,closed_at
%%entity RefundRequest help: A controlled request to return part or all of a captured payment, retaining approval and processing evidence.
%%entity RefundRequest icon: ReceiptText
%%field RefundRequest.payment_id help: Captured payment from which the authorized return is made.
%%field RefundRequest.work_order_id help: Completed or disputed work order underlying the requested refund.
